{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"3664f1c6a9f92448","name":"card_unit_1st_grenadier_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/units/card_unit_1st_grenadier_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"1st GRENADIER REGIMENT","text":"Enemy units that damage anything but this unit are destroyed.","flavorText":"The 1st Grenadier Regiment was part of the Polish 1st Grenadier Division during WWII. The division was formed in France in 1939 after Poland’s defeat in the initial German invasion as a part of the Polish Army in France. The creation of Polish formations in France marked the beginnings of the Polish Armed Forces in the West. Composed of Polish soldiers who had fled to France and of Polish workers who had migrated to France before the war, the division was led by General Bronisław Duch and became the largest Polish unit in the French Army, with more than 16,000 members. The division saw significant action in the Battle of France in 1940, where it held defensive positions and inflicted losses on the advancing German forces. However, after suffering heavy casualties and facing encirclement, the division was ultimately ordered to disband and flee to prevent capture. During the Battle of France, the division lost approximately 5,200 men, but many of those who managed to escape would later join the Polish resistance or the British forces in Britain, where they continued the fight.","faction":"Poland","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":6,"operationCost":3,"attack":3,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_1st_grenadier_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_1st_grenadier_regiment_title","SourceString":"1st GRENADIER REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"1st GRENADIER REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_1st_grenadier_regiment_text","SourceString":"Enemy units that damage anything but this unit are destroyed.","LocalizedString":"Enemy units that damage anything but this unit are destroyed."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_1st_grenadier_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 1st Grenadier Regiment was part of the Polish 1st Grenadier Division during WWII. The division was formed in France in 1939 after Poland’s defeat in the initial German invasion as a part of the Polish Army in France. The creation of Polish formations in France marked the beginnings of the Polish Armed Forces in the West. Composed of Polish soldiers who had fled to France and of Polish workers who had migrated to France before the war, the division was led by General Bronisław Duch and became the largest Polish unit in the French Army, with more than 16,000 members. The division saw significant action in the Battle of France in 1940, where it held defensive positions and inflicted losses on the advancing German forces. However, after suffering heavy casualties and facing encirclement, the division was ultimately ordered to disband and flee to prevent capture. During the Battle of France, the division lost approximately 5,200 men, but many of those who managed to escape would later join the Polish resistance or the British forces in Britain, where they continued the fight.","LocalizedString":"The 1st Grenadier Regiment was part of the Polish 1st Grenadier Division during WWII. The division was formed in France in 1939 after Poland’s defeat in the initial German invasion as a part of the Polish Army in France. The creation of Polish formations in France marked the beginnings of the Polish Armed Forces in the West. Composed of Polish soldiers who had fled to France and of Polish workers who had migrated to France before the war, the division was led by General Bronisław Duch and became the largest Polish unit in the French Army, with more than 16,000 members. The division saw significant action in the Battle of France in 1940, where it held defensive positions and inflicted losses on the advancing German forces. However, after suffering heavy casualties and facing encirclement, the division was ultimately ordered to disband and flee to prevent capture. During the Battle of France, the division lost approximately 5,200 men, but many of those who managed to escape would later join the Polish resistance or the British forces in Britain, where they continued the fight."},"operationCost":3,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamage"],"draftBaseWeight":0.8,"hasGuard":true,"exileNation":"EFactionEnum::France","Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Poland/Winter_2024/t_1st_grenadier_regiment.t_1st_grenadier_regiment","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/1st_GRENADIER_REGIMENT.1st_GRENADIER_REGIMENT","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":368.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_1st_grenadier_regiment_photo","SourceString":"Men of the 1st Grenadier Division of the Polish Army in France, 3 May 1940.","LocalizedString":"Men of the 1st Grenadier Division of the Polish Army in France, 3 May 1940."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"","Key":"0DBC5F184A8F0CFAA1A9D6BB449E2AC6","SourceString":"Infantry","LocalizedString":"Infantry"},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryS'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryS.46"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeLight_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeLight.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""},"threat_level":0.3},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"Execut